 "note": "Churchill Park, Busselton: the buildings along the north side of the harness-racing track and oval, from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026). West to east: the old grandstand (a long low-pitched roof over the seating, green-and-white striped valance along the front, a pale corrugated roof over the rooms behind), a small stewards' tower in front of it, a flat-roofed link, two big pale Colorbond halls with gable ends (one is Churchill Park Hall), a green-roofed gabled building at the east end, and on the apron by the track two banks of open concrete terraces and a green open-fronted shelter. Front = the track side (south-south-east); the street runs behind them on the north. Metres: x west to east, y north from the valance.",
